  "meteorological_explanation": "In tropical Singapore, convective thunderstorms form highly localized cells with diameters of 2-3 km. When a storm cell drops >=50mm directly over a gauge, inverse-distance-weighting (IDW) from neighbours 3-5 km away severely underestimates the peak rain, causing low interpolation recall (~59%). When the nearest neighbour is <2.5 km away, recall improves, proving that spatial basis risk is driven by convective cell scale relative to inter-gauge spacing."
